# SUPERSEDED RUN, KEPT AS A RECORD.  The first implementation of lr_intervals had a defect: with few draws the
# search over multipliers reached a nearly infeasible inner problem, the Newton iteration ran off to a saturated
# point, and a negative Newton decrement passed the convergence test; the resulting "upper bound" was nonsense
# (for example -2.9e13).  In this run 22 of 2 800 repetitions of method L-all (two cells at N = 4000) were refused
# by the certificate as "void" because L > U; other repetitions at N = 4000 may carry wrong intervals that were
